**Motion findings:** motion instants — blade approach/contact ≈0–1000 ms · sawing (stop-motion steps, object rotating to horizontal) ≈1000–4000 ms · flesh extrusion onset bracketed between 2000 ms (absent) and 3000 ms (present) — i.e. flesh appears during the LATE saw, progressively, NOT only at completion · blade exit + closed-seam hold ≈4000–5000 ms. Holds — none long inside the window; the closing state (closed halves, green seam) holds at CP5 into the next technique. No dissolve; the substitution is covered by blade + hands throughout.
**Sub-beats:** SB-A present + blade approach (0–~1000 ms) · SB-B saw steps, shell only (≈1000–~2500 ms, flesh onset bracketed 2000–3000) · SB-C saw completion with progressive flesh extrusion (≈2500–4000 ms) · SB-D blade gone, closed halves with green seam, held (≈4000–5000 ms).

### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Outer-object identity (CONFIG data): name, shell fill/highlight/shadow, segmentation columns × rows, body width/height, head (lever/pin) presence + colours — the thing being halved.
2. Inner-flesh identity (CONFIG data): name, flesh fill, flesh-light fill, skin-rim colour/width — what the cut reveals.
3. Blade: length, width, fill, edge colour, angle, travel distance, saw-step count, stroke amplitude (the back-and-forth inside each step).
4. Hands-as-shapes: grip shape fill (skin tone), size, positions (holder + guider), presence per phase.
5. Timing: present duration, saw start/duration, flesh-onset fraction of the saw, part/seam phase start/duration, hold, total duration.
6. Flesh geometry: extrusion width growth, seam-line width at close, flesh-face reveal fraction at part.
7. Ground/board: board fill, plank line colour/count, plate dressing presence (deferred — see §2.5).
8. Scale/position: object centre, object rotation (upright → horizontal tilt during saw), stage size.
9. Easing/step form: saw progress is STEPPED (stop-motion quantization), part phase eased.

